# Console tour: what a workspace actually gets after the install videos end.
# Source is a console screencast (console-shot-rig scenes/console-tour.mjs),
# not a terminal cast — VIDEO= instead of CAST=.
#
# Take v4. Earlier takes are why this file has warnings: v1 had a full
# `apikey:<uuid>` on the Approvals card, and its captions described a Policies
# screen the scene never recorded. The rig now masks credential identifiers as
# well as emails and aborts rather than record unmasked — but VERIFY ON REAL
# FRAMES AT NATIVE RESOLUTION before every publish. The identity column and the
# X-ray session meta line are the two places identifiers actually render.
#
# The Policies beat is deliberately absent; see scenes/console-tour.mjs.
#
# Two things the captions must dodge, both verified in this take:
#   44.4-49.4 (master clock) the Runs table is still sorted by STARTED — the
#     re-sort only lands at 49.45, so no "sorted by cost" caption before then.
#   loading states at 8.2, 26.7, 43.4 and 59.5.
VIDEO=console-tour-raw.mp4
# The rig captures on change, so a trailing static dwell emits no frames and the
# mp4 just ends. The per-step breakdown — the payoff — got 0.65s. Hold it.
TAIL_PAD=4
FITW=1920
FITH=1080
TITLE1='What you get after the install'
TITLE2='every agent, every call, one console'
HOOK='the shared console'
OUTRO2='connect a workspace — free to start'
OUTRO_URL='cloud.agenticcontrolplane.com'
THUMB_TITLE='Every agent call, one console'
THUMB_TAG='CONSOLE'
THUMB_T=61
SHORT_CROP=1150:1080:110:0
SHORT_START=57
SHORT_END=66
